    "created_at": "2025-03-20T20:48:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-03-20T20:48:08Z",
    "body": "I think the main problem here is that we don't support paths and only the key of the object in the first level.\n\n```ts\nconst groupsKey = env.AUTH_OIDC_GROUPS_ATTRIBUTE;\n// Groups from oidc provider are provided from the profile, it's not typed.\nif (profile && groupsKey in profile && Array.isArray(profile[groupsKey])) {\n\tawait synchronizeGroupsWithExternalForUserAsync(db, user.id, profile[groupsKey] as string[]);\n}\n```\n\nSo we would need to create a method that recursivly reads out the value like:\n\n```ts\nconst valueInPath = (obj: Record<string, unknown>, path: string) => {\n\tconst [nextKey, ...subPath] = path.split(\".\");\n\t\n\tconst next = obj[nextKey];\n\tif (subPath.length === 0) return next;\n\tif (typeof next !== \"object\") throw new Error(\"Failed to extract object in path\");\n\tif (next === null) throw new Error(\"Failed to extract object in path\");\n\treturn valueInPath(next, subPath.join('.'));\n};\n\n\n```",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
